.TH FLATSPKG 1 "2026-10-29" "flatspkg 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flatspkg \- interactive terminal manager for Flatpak applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flatspkg
.RB [ \-u | \-\-update-cache ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-l \| LANG | \-\-lang=LANG ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flatspkg
is an interactive terminal application manager written in C. It uses
.BR fzf (1)
to browse and select applications from the Flathub remote, and invokes
.BR flatpak (1)
to install, uninstall, and update applications.
.PP
The main menu provides Install, Remove, Update, and Exit actions. Multiple
applications can be selected in the installation and removal selectors.
Installations are invoked with Flatpak's automatic confirmation option;
uninstallations are invoked without that option and may prompt for
confirmation.
.PP
The Flathub application catalog is cached in
.I $HOME/.cache/flatspkg-flathub.cache
and refreshed when absent, empty, or more than 24 hours old. The
.B \-u
option forces a refresh. After attempting the refresh, the program continues
to the interactive menu; if refresh fails, a previously usable cache may
still be used.
.PP
Translations for Brazilian Portuguese, Spanish, French, and German are
embedded in the executable; English is the default. The language can be
forced with
.BR \-l / \-\-lang ,
or detected from the environment. No external locale files, gettext
library, or language packs are required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u , \ \-\-update-cache
Regenerate the local Flathub application cache before opening the menu.
Without this option, the cache is regenerated if it is missing, empty, or
more than 24 hours old. This option does not exit after refreshing; the
interactive menu is opened afterward.
.TP
.BR \-v , \ \-\-version
Print the program name and version to standard output, then exit. This option
is processed before runtime dependency checks.
.TP
.BR \-l \ LANG , \ \-\-lang= LANG
Force the interface language. Accepted values are
.BR pt ,
.BR pt_BR ,
.BR pt-BR ,
.BR es ,
.BR fr ,
.BR de ,
and
.BR en ,
case-insensitively. The short form is
.BR \-l LANG ;
the long form accepts either
.B \-\-lang LANG
or
.BR \-\-lang= LANG .
.TP
.BR \-h , \ \-\-help
Print a short usage summary to standard output, then exit. This option is
processed before runtime dependency checks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to determine the cache path. Required for the normal application flow;
if unset, the program exits with an error. The help and version options exit
before this value is needed.
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
If set and nonempty, takes precedence over
.B LANG .
Only the first entry is used when it contains a colon-separated list.
.TP
.B LANG
Locale used for language detection when
.B LANGUAGE
is unset or empty. The program strips encoding and modifier suffixes. The
language selection is based on the language prefix; unrecognized languages
fall back to English.
.PP
An explicit language supplied with
.B \-l
or
.B \-\-lang
takes precedence over both environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/flatspkg-flathub.cache
Cached, formatted list of applications from Flathub. The cache is refreshed
when missing, empty, or more than 24 hours old, or when explicitly requested
with
.BR \-u .
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.BR flatpak (1)
Required for catalog queries and Flatpak operations.
.TP
.BR fzf (1)
Required for the interactive selectors.
.PP
Both executables must be available in
.BR PATH .
The
.B \-h
and
.B \-v
options can be used without these runtime dependencies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The help or version was printed, or the interactive menu completed or was
dismissed.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown option was supplied, a required language argument is missing, an
unsupported language was selected, the normal flow cannot determine
.BR HOME ,
or a required runtime dependency is unavailable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B flatspkg
Start the interactive menu.
.TP
.B flatspkg --update-cache
Force-refresh the Flathub cache, then open the menu.
.TP
.B flatspkg --lang=pt_BR
Run with the Brazilian Portuguese interface.
.TP
.B LANG=fr_FR.UTF-8 flatspkg
Run with the French interface.
.TP
.B LANGUAGE=de flatspkg
Run with the German interface, even if
.B LANG
specifies another language.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR fzf (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Breno Rodrigues Alves.
